def add_assessment(self, assessment: Assessment) -> None:
    """Add an assessment to this course; names are unique within a course."""
    if assessment.weight <= 0:
        raise ValueError("an assessment needs a positive weight")
    if assessment.name in [a.name for a in self.assessments]:
        raise ValueError(f"{self.code} already has an assessment called {assessment.name}")
    self.assessments.append(assessment)
```
Explanation: Changed `self.assessment_names()` to a list comprehension `[a.name for a in self.assessments]` to avoid calling the method every time an assessment is added.

